# Componentes UI Minimalistas

## Button Component

```tsx
// Correcto - Button simple y reutilizable
interface ButtonProps {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'ghost';
  size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg';
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onClick?: () => void;
}

const Button = ({ 
  variant = 'primary', 
  size = 'md', 
  children,
  onClick 
}: ButtonProps) => {
  return (
    <button 
      className={`btn btn-${variant} btn-${size}`}
      onClick={onClick}
    >
      {children}
    </button>
  );
};

// CSS
.btn {
  border: none;
  border-radius: 6px;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-weight: 500;
  transition: all 0.2s;
}

.btn-primary {
  background: var(--color-primary);
  color: white;
}

.btn-md {
  padding: 8px 16px;
  font-size: 14px;
}
```

## Input Component

```tsx
// Correcto - Input limpio
const Input = ({ label, error, ...props }) => (
  <div className="input-group">
    {label && <label>{label}</label>}
    <input {...props} />
    {error && <span className="error">{error}</span>}
  </div>
);
```

## Reglas de Componentes

- Props simples: solo lo necesario
- Variantes limitadas: 2-3 variantes máximo
- Composable: permitir combinar componentes
- Accesible: usar roles y labels ARIA
- Estados visuales claros: hover, focus, disabled, error
